{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2182","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2182","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2182\",\"parent_revision\":\"2ad563cd29e1ed383f53d517c091726ee03ac2bd\",\"root_revision\":\"28b1669cd9e6e33a570113a207438f789bd8a78289803362fc3633686ce57234\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **worker preflight self-check + structured worker-report contract (5 self-review entries)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 pattern: Worker agent runs preflight self-check; worker-report.v1 contract requires 5 self-review entries (v4.3+, source CLAUDE.md)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Directly improves observability and reliability of the SAM execution loop. Downstream consumers (`forensic-review`, `contract-verification`, `complete-implementation`) currently must re-read diffs to understand what a worker did. This item provides a machine-readable summary. Complements #1857 (AC external gate) but is independently valuable. P1 is appropriate.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Affects: `task-worker.md` (emits report), `subagent-contract/SKILL.md` (schema definition), `task_status_hook.py` (parse + store), `sam_schema/core/` (new Pydantic model)\\n- Consumers unblocked: `forensic-review`, `contract-verification`, `complete-implementation` gain machine-readable worker output without diff re-analysis\\n- Bottleneck: Without the report, the AC gate (#1857) cannot consume structured worker attestation \u2014 the two items are coupled at the data model level\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `forensic-review` can query `artifact_read(worker-report)` instead of re-reading diffs\\n- `complete-implementation` can verify AC attestation fields directly\\n- Deferred work and risks become visible to orchestrators before they discover them the hard way\\n- Provides an audit trail: who changed what, what tests ran, what was deferred, what risks remain\\n- Enables #1857 AC gate to consume structured per-AC attestation objects rather than free-text concerns\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter a task-worker completes a task, querying `artifact_list(issue_number=N)` returns an entry with `artifact_type='worker-report'`. Reading it via `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type='worker-report')` returns a JSON object containing exactly the 5 required fields: `files_modified`, `tests_run`, `acceptance_criteria_attestation`, `deferred_work`, and `risks_or_followups`. The report is present regardless of whether the worker used the SubagentStop hook path or the inline `sam_task(state=complete)` path.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target observable state when done:\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/worker_report.py` exists \u2014 a Pydantic v2 model defining `WorkerReport` with the 5 required fields. Schema can be validated via `python -c 'from sam_schema.core.worker_report import WorkerReport; WorkerReport.model_validate({...})'`.\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` contains a `worker-report.v1` section defining the 5-field schema contract.\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` instructs workers to emit `<worker_report>...</worker_report>` JSON before calling `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')`.\\n4. `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` parses the `<worker_report>` block and calls `artifact_register(issue_number, 'worker-report', content=...)` on SubagentStop.\\n5. Running a task through `dh:implement-feature` produces a queryable `worker-report` artifact.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/worker_report.py` exists and exports a `WorkerReport` Pydantic v2 model with fields: `files_modified: list[str]`, `tests_run: list[dict]`, `acceptance_criteria_attestation: list[dict]`, `deferred_work: list[dict]`, `risks_or_followups: list[dict]`.\\n2. `uv run python -c 'from sam_schema.core.worker_report import WorkerReport; r = WorkerReport(files_modified=[\\\"a.py\\\"], tests_run=[], acceptance_criteria_attestation=[], deferred_work=[], risks_or_followups=[]); print(r.model_dump_json())'` exits 0 and prints valid JSON.\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` contains a `worker-report.v1` schema block with all 5 required fields documented.\\n4. `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` contains instructions requiring `<worker_report>` JSON emission before `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')`.\\n5. `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler: when `<worker_report>` block is found in agent transcript, calls `artifact_register(issue_number, 'worker-report', content=parsed_json)`.\\n6. After running a test task through `dh:implement-feature`: `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_list(issue_number=N)` output includes a `worker-report` entry and `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type='worker-report')` returns content with all 5 fields.\\n7. Existing `task_status_hook.py` tests continue to pass (`uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/ -x`).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | `/dh:subagent-contract` \u2014 target SKILL.md for schema definition |\\n| Skill | `/dh:start-task` \u2014 shows how SubagentStop hook context flows |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop handler to extend |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Pydantic v2 model patterns to follow |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 agent file to update |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` \u2014 schema section target |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `artifact_register` implementation (lines ~2387+) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/` \u2014 test suite to extend |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None blocking (standalone schema addition)\\n- Complements: #1857 (Add acceptance-criteria validation gate before task-worker marks complete) \u2014 that item's AC gate can consume `acceptance_criteria_attestation` from the worker report once this schema exists\\n- Blocks: #1857 at the data model level \u2014 the AC gate needs structured per-AC attestation objects\\n- Related: #1944 (stalled-task detection), #2183 (Advisor agent) \u2014 both benefit from richer worker output signals\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Estimated 3\u20135 focused tasks:\\n1. Add `sam_schema/core/worker_report.py` Pydantic model (small)\\n2. Update `subagent-contract/SKILL.md` with schema section (small)\\n3. Update `task-worker.md` with report emission instructions (small)\\n4. Extend `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler to parse and store (medium \u2014 requires parsing `<worker_report>` XML-style block from transcript, calling `artifact_register`)\\n5. Add/extend tests in `test_task_status_hook/` (medium)\\n\\nNo new hook infrastructure needed \u2014 extends existing SubagentStop path.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. All required files are accessible and all interfaces are live.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: 5-field `worker-report.v1` schema, task-worker update, hook parsing, artifact storage |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | In-scope and out-of-scope explicitly stated; complements #1857 (external AC gate) |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `sam_task`, `artifact_register`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_read` \u2014 live and documented in `backlog_core/server.py` |\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | PEP 723 hook scripts, `ruamel.yaml`, Pydantic v2 \u2014 established patterns in `sam_schema/core/models.py` and `task_status_hook.py` |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `task_status_hook.py`, `subagent-contract/SKILL.md`, `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 all located and read |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal defined: `artifact_list` + `artifact_read` shows `worker-report` entry with all 5 fields; Pydantic validation |\\n\\nNo MISSING conditions. No BLOCKED workstreams.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` defines the universal task-worker agent. The agent is instructed to call `sam_task(action='claim')`, execute, and call `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')`. It may emit a `<concerns>` block (read by `implement-feature/SKILL.md` step 4), but the concerns block is optional and unstructured \u2014 no schema requires the worker to attest to specific self-review checks before declaring complete.\\n\\nThe `dh:subagent-contract` skill (`plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`) describes a generic subagent contract but does not define a `worker-report.v1` schema with required self-review entries.\\n\\nIssue #1857 (Add acceptance-criteria validation gate before task-worker marks complete) addresses the *external* gate \u2014 verifying AC are met before completion is recorded. This proposal addresses the *internal* gate \u2014 the worker self-attesting via a structured report on what it changed, what tests it ran, what it deferred, and what risks remain. The two are complementary: the AC gate consumes the worker report when present.\\n\\nWithout a structured worker report, downstream consumers (forensic-review, contract-verification, complete-implementation) have no machine-readable summary of what the worker actually did versus claimed; they must re-read the diff.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` defines `worker-report.v1` with 5 required self-review fields:\\n\\n1. `files_modified`: array of paths (verifiable via `git diff --name-only`)\\n2. `tests_run`: command(s) executed and exit codes\\n3. `acceptance_criteria_attestation`: per-AC `{id, status: met|partial|deferred, evidence}` objects\\n4. `deferred_work`: explicit list of items not done with reason (or empty array)\\n5. `risks_or_followups`: array of `{description, suggested_followup_issue}` (or empty array)\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` is updated to require emitting `<worker_report>...</worker_report>` JSON matching the v1 schema before calling `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')`. The hook `task_status_hook.py` (PostToolUse + SubagentStop) parses the report and stores it as a `worker-report` artifact via `artifact_register(issue_number, \\\"worker-report\\\", content=...)`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun a task via `dh:implement-feature` for a small plan. After the worker completes, query: `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_list(issue_number=N)` \u2014 output includes a `worker-report` entry. Read it: `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"worker-report\\\")` \u2014 content contains all 5 required fields per the v1 schema.\\n\\nSchema file `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/worker_report.py` exists and validates the JSON via Pydantic.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f6cf19e1653ea54ec92bbca4be0b0a54c13d4c70b48254b15618a940b1fbca9d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg3SrQ\"}"}